From: WL2GO
Subject: Expose the hybrid station list and Message Pickup Stations on the HTTP API

Radio-Only operation -- Winlink's hybrid network, which keeps mail moving over
RF when the internet is down -- needs two things from the CMS: which RMS
gateways are hybrid stations, and which of them hold the operator's mail (the
Message Pickup Stations). Upstream implements both only as CLI subcommands
(cli/mps.go). These routes expose the same cmsapi calls to the client that
spawned this process, with the same three-station limit, so that client never
needs an api.winlink.org access key of its own:

  GET    /api/wl2go/hybrid_stations
  GET    /api/wl2go/mps
  POST   /api/wl2go/mps   {"callsign": "..."}
  DELETE /api/wl2go/mps   (clears every entry; the CMS has no single delete)

The password is the configured secure_login_password, as the existing
winlink-account handlers use. Errors are JSON with a "kind" of network, cms or
request, so the client can tell "offline" from "refused". Every route sits
behind the 0001 guard.
---
